The implementation foundation was the user-provided kimi-code-main checkout.

The retained pi-tui library is Moonshot AI's fork of earendil-works/pi:
https://github.com/earendil-works/pi
Copyright (c) 2025 Mario Zechner. Licensed under the MIT License;
see packages/pi-tui/LICENSE (also dist/LICENSE.pi-tui in the built output).

The embedded WebP decoder comes from @jsquash/webp, copyright 2023
jamsinclair, Apache-2.0, and includes libwebp, distributed under its BSD
license. See third-party-licenses/ in the source distribution and the
corresponding LICENSE.jsquash-webp and LICENSE.libwebp files in dist/.

Standalone builds include the @mariozechner/clipboard native binding, an
MIT-licensed fork of @crosscopy/clipboard. Source and license information:
https://github.com/badlogic/clipboard and https://github.com/CrossCopy/clipboard.

CoderAI adapts the terminal host, application identity and storage defaults,
startup probing, default approval policy, built-in product skills, prompt
wording and packaging. Provider names, OAuth identifiers and persisted Kimi
engine formats are retained for compatibility. The original checkout is not
needed at build time or runtime. External npm dependencies retain their own
licenses in their installed packages.
